Q: I have spondylosis and osteoporosis and my doctor requires me to take collagen as part of treatment. But I have been a vegetarian for 14 years. Can I take normal collagen?
Sources: Metaphysics Q&A Vol 3 (EN) | Buddhism Q&A (EN) | Metaphysics Q&A Vol 3 (EN) · types: qa_metaphysics,qa_general,introduction
  ✓ substantial reply (>600 chars)
  ✗ ends cleanly (punctuation/emoji, not mid-word)
  ✓ answers the vegetarian-collagen question
  ✓ final text passes guard (0 residual)
--- reply ---
Keeping a vegetarian diet for 14 years is not a small thing 🙏 I understand the difficulty you're facing now.

**Master Lu did address supplements containing animal ingredients directly.** In the Buddhism Q&A he said:

> When you consume any medicine or health supplements that contain ingredients such as gelatine or fish oil, if your body does not reject the taste, then perhaps you have not reached the level where you are completely observing your precepts. However, it would still be best to avoid consuming such products as they contain animal by-products.

So the guidance is clear: **it is best to avoid animal-based collagen if there is any alternative.** Please talk to your doctor first — ask whether a plant-based / vegan collagen supplement, or calcium + vitamin D + protein from soy products, can serve the same purpose for your bones. Very often there is an option. Master Lu also taught that soy products are high in protein and that we should take care of our body, because Bodhisattvas want us to have a healthy body so we can practise better.

**If your doctor confirms there is genuinely no alternative** and you truly have no choice, the principle Master Lu gave for such situations is about your intention. In a similar case he taught:

> Under extreme circumstances when you have no choice but to consume those vegetables, you should say to Guan Yin Bodhisattva in your mind that you are consuming these vegetables because you have no choice, and you do not want to eat them at all.

The same spirit applies here — in your heart, tell Guan Yin Bodhisattva your full name, that you are taking this only as medicine because you have no choice, and that you have absolutely no desire for it. Taking something as medicine under doctor's orders, with no craving in the heart, is not the same as breaking a precept out of desire.

Alongside this, you can recite for your bones:

📿 **Great Compassion Mantra** — 3 to 7 times daily
Before reciting say: *"May the Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva bless me, [your full name], with good health and heal the illness in my spine and bones."*

Buddhism and medicine work together — please continue with your doctor's treatment 🙏

May I ask, are you already doing daily recitation, or would you like me to help you start?

*Reference: Buddhism Q&A — Frequently Asked Questions About Practising Buddhism*

